# LaTeX, as written

LaTeX's own commands, as a `@begin(tabbing)` environment; cells carry inline
formatting and maths, and `\a'` / `\a=` are the accents.

@begin(tabbing)
*Symbol* \= $x^2 + y^2$ \= /the circle/ \\
*Name* \> $r$ \> radius \\
Caf\a'e \> $\bar{x}$ \> the m\a=ean
@end(tabbing)

The same commands inside the fence, with `\pushtabs`, `\poptabs`, `\kill` and
`\\[len]`:

```tabbing
Name: \= Street: \= Phone \\[2pt] Alice \> 12 Oak \> 555 \\
\pushtabs
A much longer column \= x \kill
\> temporary \\
\poptabs
\> back
```
